-- title:
--   Fontaine–Hodge membership at a twisted Tate level
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal{O}$, such that $\mathcal{O}$ is an algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ with $\ker(\mathcal{O}\to\mathbb{Z}/p)=(p)$, and such that $\mathcal{O}$ is $(p)$-adically complete. Fix $r$ and a Honda system $H_1$ on $\mathcal{O}^r$ for the element $p$ (maps $F,V$ with $FV=VF=p$, together with a submodule $H_1.L$ satisfying the divisibility, generation and torsion-freeness conditions of [`Deformation.HondaSystem`](def/Dieudonne_DatumAndHonda.html#L73)), a tower $G$ of finite cocommutative Hopf $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebras with transition bialgebra maps $s$, additive maps $\pi_v:\mathcal{O}^r\to$ [`Deformation.DieudonneModule (ZMod p) p (G v)`](def/Dieudonne_WittHomColimit.html#L234), and split coordinates $\mathcal{S}$ for these data which are `Lawful`. Let $\Phi$ be a commutative $\mathcal{S}.d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal{O}$, and let $c_2$ assign to each level $v$ a $\mathcal{S}.d$-tuple in $\mathcal{S}.\mathrm{Et}\,v\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}\mathcal{S}.\mathrm{Et}\,v$ with all entries in the ideal generated by $p$. Assume the logarithm-additivity hypothesis `hLOGA`: for every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $g$ in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor and which is $(p)$-adically complete, every level $v$, every pair of $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps $f,f':\mathcal{S}.\mathrm{Et}\,v\to g$, every pair of tuples $x,x'$ with entries in the radical of $(p)g$, and every $i$, the sum of the $p$-adic series [`Deformation.PLoc.wSeries`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineFunctor.html#L233) of the coefficients $\mathcal{S}.a\,i$ evaluated adically at the $\Phi$-sum of $x$, $x'$ and the images of $c_2\,v$ under $f\otimes f'$, and of the series of the $(f\otimes f')\circ\Delta$-images of the $\mathcal{S}.\hat c\,i\,k\,v$, equals the sum of the two corresponding expressions formed from $(x,f)$ and from $(x',f')$ separately. Fix a level $v$ and a commutative ring $L_v$ which is a Hopf $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module, together with an $\mathcal{O}$-bialgebra map $\iota_v:\mathcal{S}.\mathrm{Et}\,v\to L_v$ and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\Psi_v$ from the power series ring in $\mathcal{S}.d$ variables to $L_v$ such that each $\Psi_v(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p)L_v$, $\Psi_v$ is given by adic evaluation at the $\Psi_v(X_i)$, each $\Psi_v(X_i)$ has vanishing counit, the comultiplication of $\Psi_v(X_i)$ is the $\Phi$-twisted expression built from $\Psi_v(X_j)\otimes 1$, $1\otimes\Psi_v(X_j)$ and $(\iota_v\otimes\iota_v)(c_2\,v)$, and multiplication by $p^v$ on $L_v$ (the $p^v$-th convolution power of the identity) factors as the counit followed by the structure map. Finally let $ee$ be a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-bialgebra map from $\mathcal{S}.\mathrm{Gc}\,v\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p}\mathcal{S}.\mathrm{Ge}\,v$ to $\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}L_v$ carrying $\mathcal{S}.\kappa\,v(\bar F)\otimes 1$ to $1\otimes\Psi_v(F)$ for every power series $F$, and $1\otimes\mathcal{S}.\theta e\,v(1\otimes y)$ to $1\otimes\iota_v(y)$. Then for each $i$, the image of $\pi_v$ applied to the $i$-th vector of the basis $\mathcal{S}.\alpha$ of $H_1.L$, pushed forward along $\mathcal{S}.\Theta\,v$ followed by $ee$, lies in [`Deformation.fontaineHodge (ZMod p) p`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L272) taken with respect to the ring homomorphism underlying $\mathrm{includeRight}:L_v\to\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}L_v$, that is, it is represented at some truncation level $n$ by a primitive truncated Witt vector lying in the corresponding `fontaineKer`.
--
--   This is the final membership assertion in Fontaine's lifting theorem for $p$-divisible groups in the general connected–étale situation: the Dieudonné-module class of a basis vector of the Hodge submodule of the given Honda system, transported to the special fibre of the constructed level $L_v$, lies in the Fontaine–Hodge submodule cut out by the lift $L_v$ itself. It is the step invoked by [`Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_pDivisibleTower_bijective_map_mem_fontaineHodge_of_splitCoordinates_of_cocycle`](thm.html#Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_pDivisibleTower_bijective_map_mem_fontaineHodge_of_splitCoordinates_of_cocycle), which assembles the levels $L_v$ into a $p$-divisible tower realising the Honda system.
